      <h2>About Prison Island</h2>
      <div>Changuu (Prison Island) was purchased by the British in 1893 intending to build a prison for rebellious slaves, but became a quarantine station for yellow fever and other diseases. Today it's famous for its population of giant Aldabra tortoises (Aldabrachelys gigantea), some estimated at 150+ years old, brought from Seychelles in the 1920s. The island offers coral reef snorkeling, a small museum on quarantine history, and peacocks roaming freely. 20-minute boat ride from Stone Town. Combine with Nakupenda sandbank for a perfect half-day marine excursion.</div>
